// The finale: three springs and a wall with a single gap.
name Confluence
rule B1/S012345678
steps 5
hint Three springs. A wall with one gap divides them, and every ripple keeps what it makes.
tip Two springs above the wall, one below it. The one below leaked up through the gap.
intro Three springs behind a broken wall. This is the last ruin, and the shape in it is one you know: it is the shape you woke inside.
outro You planted the seeds where the springs rose, and the world grew back around you. It began here. So did you.
